<h1>How many people are in the Talmud, and how would we know?</h1>
<p class="lede">A name on a page of Talmud is not a person. One name can belong to several men. One
man can appear under several names. We want to work out who is who, when each one lived, and how
sure we are, starting from the text and nothing else.</p>
<p>This page does two things. It reviews the work done so far and says plainly what was wrong
with it. Then it sets out the plan from scratch: what we read, what we pull out, what we join up,
and how we check every step.</p>

